{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1244536-haunts-and-numina","id":1244536,"title":"Haunts and Numina","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-10T09:59:43-07:00","id":1244536,"title":"Haunts and Numina","content":"So: Haunts are something unique to Sin-Eaters, sort of. They work due to the hybrid nature of the Bound's \u201csoul\u201d; and ghosts, lacking such, don't have access to them.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Haunts are inspired by ghostly phenomena from various ghost stories; so it's reasonable to assume that most Haunts have counterparts among the ghostly Numina. So: what are they?<br /> <br /> Haunts: Boneyard, Caul, Curse, Dirge, Marionette, Memoria, Oracle, Rage, Shroud, Tomb.<br /> <br /> Caul and Shroud are especially dependent on the dual nature of the Bound; as well, Shroud is basically \u201cI become ghost-like, and eventually can attain a Twilight state and use Manifestations\u201d. I'm not 100% sure; but I think that there's little if anything in terms of Numina where those two Haunts are concerned.<br /> <br /> But that still leaves Boneyard, Curse, Dirge, Marionette, Memorial, Oracle, Rage, and Tomb. <br /> <br /> Numina: Anchor Jump, Awe, Blast, Descend, Drain, Emotional Aura, Empower Ghost, Engulf, Firestarter, Hallucination, Host Jump, Implant Mission, Innocuous, Left-Handed Spanner, Moliate, Omen Trance, Pathfinder, Proxy, Puppeteer, Rapture, Regenerate, Seek, Speed, Sign, Stalwart, Telekinesis.<br /> <br /> Note that a few of these are limited to high-Rank ghosts, and as such probably aren't a factor here. Empower Ghost, for instance, is a Kerberos Numen that's unlikely to be seen in the living world. <br /> <br /> Work calls, so I'll have to leave it here for now. Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T10:09:19-07:00","id":1244539,"title":"","content":"I'd argue that Manifestations should be included in this list as the other Ghostly Power Set. I don't have the list of those in front of me atm. But I actually see some metaphysical parallels between some aspects of The Caul and the manifestation The Bargain <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b><br /> OK so the Manifestations in the manuscript are:<br /> Twilight form, Avernian Gateway, Bargain, Claim, Descend, Discorperate, Fetter, Image, Materialize, Possess, Unfetter.<br /> <br /> <br /> Quick side note: I don't really get the difference between Numina and Manifestations. I get that Manifestations are for the interaction beyond Twilight and that certain Manifestation conditions need to be present. But not all manifestations require a manifestation condition and there are plenty of Numina that also effect things beyond Twilight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":654,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","user":"xiongrey","date":". 08-10-2018, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T10:40:38-07:00","id":1244551,"title":"","content":"Well, Rage is definitely Blast.<br /> <br /> I'd say Shroud would be related to manifestation related, specifically Discorporate and Avernian Gate. Innocuous could fit as a numina related.<br /> <br /> Caul too has echoes of Moliate.<br /> <br /> Boneyard I'd see related to Seek, Pathfinder, maybe Speed. Anchor jump. Maybe Telekinesis.<br /> <br /> Marionette would be Host Jump, Telekinesis, Left Handed Spanner, Implant Mission.<br /> <br /> Dirge and Memoriam have Emotional Aura, Implant Mission, Rapture, and Sign. Memoriam includes Omen Trance as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T13:21:50-07:00","id":1244603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1244536-haunts-and-numina?p=1244539#post1244539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue that Manifestations should be included in this list as the other Ghostly Power Set. I don't have the list of those in front of me atm. But I actually see some metaphysical parallels between some aspects of The Caul and the manifestation The Bargain <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b><br /> OK so the Manifestations in the manuscript are:<br /> Twilight form, Avernian Gateway, Bargain, Claim, <s>Descend</s>, Discorperate, Fetter, Image, Materialize, Possess, Unfetter.<br /> <br /> <br /> Quick side note: I don't really get the difference between Numina and Manifestations. I get that Manifestations are for the interaction beyond Twilight and that certain Manifestation conditions need to be present. But not all manifestations require a manifestation condition and there are plenty of Numina that also effect things beyond Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Descend is a Numina, but was a Manifestation. The manuscript still retains it listed as a Manifestation, but that is a mistake.<br /> <br /> Manifestations interact with Manifestation Conditions. Numina don't. That's basically it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /